{
  "dom_id": "step-q66551",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "${2}^{x}=32$ is equivalent to",
  "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a={b}^{x}$ is equivalent to ${log}_{b}⁡a=x$\n\nIf we compare ${2}^{x}=32$ with $a={b}^{x},$ we get $a=32$ and $b=2.$\n\nTherefore, the equation ${2}^{x}=32$ is equivalent to ${log}_{2}⁡32=x.$",
